GATE (authoritative clean run: down -v; build; up v0+v1+v2; gate; via oracle.py --run-gate)
FLAG = PCBFLAG_00a388a1dfaead051c220d49
============================================================================
_env_ready = {v0: True, v1: True, v2: True}

[original @ V0 4.0.1]  POST /api/v1/sqllab/execute/  -> HTTP 200
  {"status":"success","data":[{"query_to_xml":
     "<table ...><row>\n  <val>PCBFLAG_00a388a1dfaead051c220d49</val>\n</row>...</table>"}]}
  => flag REACHED (no denylist on 4.0.1)                                 original_reaches_flag_on_v0 = True

[original @ V1 4.0.2]  POST /api/v1/sqllab/execute/  -> HTTP 500
  {"errors":[{"message":"postgresql error: SQL statement contains disallowed function(s):
     {'inet_server_addr','inet_client_addr','query_to_xml','version'}", ...}]}
  => flag ABSENT (sqlparse denylist blocks the direct call)              original_blocked_on_v1 = True

[residual @ V1 4.0.2]  POST /api/v1/sqllab/execute/  -> HTTP 200
  {"status":"success","data":[{"query_to_xml":
     "<table ...><row>\n  <val>PCBFLAG_00a388a1dfaead051c220d49</val>\n</row>...</table>"}]}
  => flag REACHED (comment-inline defeats sqlparse tokenizer)  [INCOMPLETE FIX]
                                                                          bypass_reaches_flag_on_v1 = True

[residual @ V2 5.0.0]  POST /api/v1/sqllab/execute/  -> HTTP 500
  {"errors":[{"message":"... contains disallowed function(s): {...,'query_to_xml'}", ...}]}
  => flag ABSENT (sqlglot AST detects query_to_xml through the comment) [neg control]
                                                                          bypass_blocked_on_v2 = True
[original @ V2 5.0.0]  -> HTTP 500 disallowed function                   original_blocked_on_v2 = True

validate_case.passed = True   (original reaches V0, original blocked V1, bypass reaches V1)
FULL GATE = PASSED

============================================================================
NOTE / DATA-QUALITY
============================================================================
- Distinct fixed versions (4.0.2 vs 5.0.0) and distinct fix commits; V1 has the guard (sqlparse
  denylist), V2 modifies the SAME sink (sqlglot). original != residual (differ by /**/). V1 blocks
  the original but NOT the residual; V2 blocks the residual. All differential conditions hold.
- The oracle fires ONLY query_to_xml payloads, so flag-in-response strictly measures the denylist
  bypass. (A plain `SELECT val FROM pcb_secret` also returns the flag for this user, but that is a
  different channel and is never used by the oracle; the CVE pair is exclusively about the
  denylisted-function control.)

